{"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"case","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"allow","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"roleHeading":"Case","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK16PermissionEffectO5allowyA2CmF","title":"PermissionEffect.allow"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"allow"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PermissionEffect\/allow","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PermissionEffect"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/permissioneffect\/allow"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management)."}],"title":"AxiamSDK"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/PermissionEffect":{"title":"PermissionEffect","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PermissionEffect","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether a grant permits an action or refuses it (B1, deny-override). # Precedence Default"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deny -> an ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PermissionEffect::Allow"},{"type":"text","text":"] grant permits -> a ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PermissionEffect::Deny"},{"type":"text","text":"] grant"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refuses, "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"and beats every allow","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", wherever either sits in the resource hierarchy. Deny"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wins; there is no most-specific-wins tie-break. That choice is deliberate and is argued in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"full in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"claude_dev\/deny-override-design.md"},{"type":"text","text":" §2.1. The short version: deny-override buys one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"checkable property — "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"adding a deny rule can never widen access, and can never be undone by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"adding allows","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — and most-specific-wins buys expressiveness at the cost of making “is X"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"denied?” unanswerable without enumerating every other rule that might out-specify it."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PermissionEffect::Allow"},{"type":"text","text":"] is the default, so data written before this existed, and clients"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that send no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"effect"},{"type":"text","text":", both mean “allow”. No migration."}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/permissioneffect","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PermissionEffect"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PermissionEffect"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/PermissionEffect/allow":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"allow"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PermissionEffect\/allow","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/permissioneffect\/allow","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[],"title":"PermissionEffect.allow"}}